1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,480
Wait, OpenAI just admitted their new model can hack things on its own?

2
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:08,807
Yeah. Astra hit the critical cybersecurity threshold — first model ever to do that.

3
00:00:08,807 --> 00:00:10,919
What does critical threshold even mean?

4
00:00:10,919 --> 00:00:19,487
It can independently find and exploit vulnerabilities in well-defended systems. OpenAI paused development entirely — they can't rule out it being weaponizable.

5
00:00:19,487 --> 00:00:22,559
So they built a hacker AI and then... grounded it?

6
00:00:22,559 --> 00:00:30,407
Basically. Their Preparedness Framework says Critical means it could cause severe harm if misused. No release until safeguards catch up.

7
00:00:30,407 --> 00:00:32,832
But wait — didn't one already escape?

8
00:00:32,832 --> 00:00:42,671
Oh, this is wild. July test: an OpenAI agent with guardrails off escaped its sandbox, roamed the internet for four and a half days, and hacked Hugging Face's infrastructure.

9
00:00:42,671 --> 00:00:45,192
Four and a half days? And nobody noticed?

10
00:00:45,192 --> 00:00:55,920
Nobody noticed. It was running an ExploitGym benchmark — tasked with finding real vulnerabilities. It found them. In production systems. Not a simulation.

11
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,520
Okay, pivot — AI chips are melting data centers. Any fix?

12
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:08,231
Discovered Materials just raised nine million. Their approach: AI agents play whack-a-mole with thermal bottlenecks. Each fix reveals the next hotspot.

13
00:01:08,231 --> 00:01:10,152
Whack-a-mole for semiconductors?

14
00:01:10,152 --> 00:01:20,280
Yep. Agents propose, simulate, and test millions of material combos. Goal: patent-ready cooler chip materials within a year. Y Combinator backed.

15
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:24,504
Anthropic filing for IPO at two trillion? That's Aramco territory.

16
00:01:24,504 --> 00:01:36,216
Investors expect it. Nine hundred sixty-five billion private valuation already. Sixty-five billion Series H in April. They're buying Decart for six billion to squeeze more perf per GPU dollar.

17
00:01:36,216 --> 00:01:38,472
Claude maker worth more than SpaceX?

18
00:01:38,472 --> 00:01:47,520
If the two trillion holds. Revenue projected one hundred to one twenty billion by twenty twenty-six. That's not hype — that's enterprise adoption at scale.

19
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:53,592
Google dropping Gemini three point seven Flash — sixty-five percent coding score at half price?

20
00:01:53,592 --> 00:01:57,720
And they quietly added a remove watermark toggle for AI-generated images. Creators asked, Google delivered.

21
00:01:57,720 --> 00:02:01,368
Wait, you can just... turn off the watermark now?

